---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import FlowShot from '../../../components/flow/FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../../../components/flow/FlowDetail.astro';
import shotRuntimeModels from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-runtime-models-shot.webp';
import detailRuntimeStorage from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-runtime-storage.webp';
---
<!-- Chapter 4: Bundled owned runtime -->
<section class="flow-runtime border-t border-border/60 bg-surface-raised/30 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-runtime">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:gap-14">
      <div>
        <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Owned local runtime</p>
        <h3 id="tour-runtime" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">Install nothing but Flow.</h3>
        <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">
          Install nothing but Flow, and you can still pull a model and run approval-gated
          agency on your own machine. That is measured, not planned: on a notarized install
          with no other AI runtime present, a 5.98 GB model was pulled and three runs were
          approved, every one served by the app's own helper. Flow's bundle carries two
          engines for about 19 MiB. The size of twenty photos.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          The bundled runtime is a floor, never a wall. Already run Ollama or LM Studio? Flow
          detects them, keeps them first class, and serves the models you already pulled in
          place. Your gigabytes are never downloaded twice.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          What Flow holds and what Flow borrows are shown as different things, because they
          are. Downloaded models are Flow's own bytes, counted against a disk allowance you
          set. Shared models are read where they already sit, and removing one from Flow's
          list leaves the original files untouched.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-dim">
          Zero-install run measured 2026-08-14 on one M3 Max, on the running build, with 399 network samples recording no connection off the machine. Loopback only.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-primary">2 engines</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">One for each common local model format on a Mac. Every layer of the model runs on the graphics chip, 29 of 29, verified.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-primary">263 a second</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Words read a second on a 7-billion-parameter model, one M3 Max. It writes at 51 words a second.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-primary">Offline</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">The engine loaded and generated with its network host pointed at a dead port. No silent network dependency.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="of-surface rounded-2xl border border-border/70 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-primary">0 bytes</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Re-downloaded when Flow served a 4.7 GB model you already pulled with another tool. No copy, no import step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- "What Flow holds vs what Flow borrows" is the claim, and it is a
         two-line distinction inside one card. Shown as a crop first, at a
         size where "nothing copied" is actually readable, then the window. -->
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowDetail
        src={detailRuntimeStorage}
        alt="Flow's Runtime card: two Downloaded models against a 4.59 GB of 20 GB allowance bar, and below them Shared models served from Ollama and LM Studio folders with nothing copied."
        caption="Downloaded is Flow's own bytes · Shared is read where it already sits"
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 46rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        glow
      />
    </div>
    <FlowShot
      class="mt-10"
      src={shotRuntimeModels}
      alt="Flow's Runtime card splitting Downloaded models, with a disk allowance bar, from Shared models served in place from other apps' folders."
      caption="The same card in place: what Flow keeps, what Flow borrows, and how much of your allowance is used."
    />
  </div>
</section>
